Selenium setup on Windows

Prerequisite
- Firefox or Google Chrome installed

1. Download and install NodeJs (https://nodejs.org/en/download/).
 
2. Create a directory for selenium project.
 
4. Download the drivers to allow WebDriver to control the browsers you want to test
   Geckodriver - (https://github.com/mozilla/geckodriver/releases/) for Firefox
   Chromedriver - (http://chromedriver.chromium.org/) for Google Chrome

5. Extract the driver to any directory you want.

6. Go to Start menu, right click Computer and click Properties

7. Click Advanced system settings

8. Click Environment Variables

9. Under System Variables, locate Path variable and Click Edit

10. Add the directory where the browser drivers are extracted and click Ok

11. Open Command Prompt (CMD), and go to your Selenium project folder,
    Create package.json "npm init" and
    run this command to install the necessary dependencies
    "npm install selenium-webdriver chai".
    For mocha run this command to install it globally
    "npm install -g mocha".

14. You can start creating test scripts.
    enter "mocha -t <timeout ms> <path/to/file>" in cmd
    to run your test scripts.

Docs:
- Selenium NodeJs (https://seleniumhq.github.io/selenium/docs/api/javascript/module/selenium-webdriver/)
- Mocha (https://mochajs.org/)
- Chai (https://www.chaijs.com/api/)
